invariant: INV-14
file: include/chapulin/cpu_cfg.h
catches: test/host-builds.sh
reason: cpu_cfg.h's x86-64 set loses CH_CPU_BMI1, so every init refuses
  the value a caller on a CPU with BMI1 states, and no session runs
  sha3_hw.c's x86-64 copy (docs/decisions.md 217). test/host-builds.sh
  reads the header for both architectures under the pinned clang and
  compares each set with the bits it writes out.

--- old
     CH_CPU_VAES | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 | CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA | CH_CPU_AVX512 |              \
     CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX | CH_CPU_BMI1)
--- new
     CH_CPU_VAES | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 | CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA | CH_CPU_AVX512 |              \
     CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX)
